<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany's Nmecha won't repeat controversial goal celebration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe51b943829f787efe4a6aeb2af6040e89965e8740d8a6abf0ffdd6a4000e93c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T11:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994--cc5ab533247b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-nmecha-won-t-repeat-controversial-goal-celebration/a-79937994?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany head coach Jürgen Klopp says that midfielder Felix Nmecha will not repeat a goal celebration that sparked controversy over the past week. Germany are set to face Serbia and the Netherlands in the Nations League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament agrees on debt-laden 2027 budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:776287455e5a2a458f7d76a0640c870454b5b064656177cb8fbe4c188ab23c42</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897--be62c4ec3578.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-agrees-on-debt-laden-2027-budget/live-79936897?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The budget committee in the Bundestag worked into the night to sign off on next year's spending plans. These include levels of new debt only eclipsed once, at the height of the COVID pandemic. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mercedes-Benz halts all further investment at German facilities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e4ed2e13727bc1d974a82376fe880634e0ae79ca7999fef8e56142601f36290</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mercedes-benz-halts-all-further-investment-at-german-facilities/a-79934509--4d8c6f3edf08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mercedes-benz-halts-all-further-investment-at-german-facilities/a-79934509?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The announcement comes as the luxury German automaker faces increasing pressure from the works council and trade unions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Police raid chapters of Gremium MC biker gang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ee0f422122c9e6d22380ee9a8c4e827929f306694fb60bf1c1d7836f1fbe72c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T09:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275--65b7228f3ec1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-police-raid-chapters-of-gremium-mc-biker-gang/live-79926275?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in southwestern Germany launched major early-morning operations against a biker gang. The state of Baden-Württemberg is outlawing three of its chapters. Meanwhile, unions are planning more strikes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8a3116dd9d7edcb4833e3e961840f7fcda30b5d4dbee5942f02e1f6b0650fa2</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Cyber attacks and hybrid warfare: Germany gives sweeping powers to its police and intelligence services</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9707d3a2a2f4b0edeff56934fd3e20f24ec21bdab5fa3aa4141fdd611aa0903</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-servic/a-79941507--8b38eb9f8681.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyber-attacks-and-hybrid-warfare-germany-gives-sweeping-powers-to-its-police-and-intelligence-services/a-79941507?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone sightings and cyberattacks have heightened security concerns. How are the police preparing to meet these challenges? And how do intelligence services plan to counter threats from both domestic and foreign sources?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Bundeswehr study exposes widespread sexual harassment in German military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a3f5ca0f32f6e4f7615efb292273a59dafcf4638dd7ffa989e84dccbeaa3e22</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T08:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359--0cec81791758.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bundeswehr-study-exposes-widespread-sexual-harassment-in-german-military/a-79926359?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sexual misconduct in the Bundeswehr is far more widespread than previously known, with younger women disproportionately affected. Defense Minister Boris Pistorius has called for a policy of "zero tolerance."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
